   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Thomas J. Carinci, Jr. to take the competitive civil\nservice examination and be placed on the eligible civil service list for\nemployment as a full-time police officer for the city of Little Falls",
    "basePrintNo": "S8333",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8333-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8333\n\nSPONSOR: SEWARD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize Thomas J. Carinci, Jr. to take the competitive civil\nservice examination and be placed on the eligible civil service list for\nemployment as a full-time police officer for the city of Little Falls\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide the city of Little Falls the opportunity to offer Mr. Carinci\na full time position with the police department upon his satisfactory\nperformance on the relevant civil service examination.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill deems Mr. Carinci eligible to sit for the compet-\nitive civil service examination for police officer and, contingent on\nhis score, shall be eligible to be placed on the list for appointment as\na full-time police officer in the city of Little Falls. Section 2\nrequires the candidate to be subject to all other relevant provisions of\nthe civil service law regarding police officers. Section 3 provides the\neffective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nCurrent law limits prospective candidates to those under the age of 35\nyears old.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe mayor and police chief of the city of Little Falls have requested\nthe latitude to hire Mr. Carinci as a full-time officer. He is currently\na part-time officer with the city and with two other police agencies in\nthe county. Due to the age ceiling in civil service law, the city is\ncurrently unable to offer him a full-time position. Mr. Carinci has\nsatisfactorily completed the police academy training regimen and meets\nall other relevant requirements. The city considers the individual high-\nly capable and valuable, and seeks the authority to consider him for a\nfull-time position.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
